  "body": "### What is the issue with the MIME Sniffing Standard?\n\nThe [resource header](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#reading-the-resource-header) is 1445 bytes, enough for an MP3 frame at 320 kbps. Sniffing AAC in ADTS (#114) needs the sync word of the next frame, and multi-channel, low-sample-rate AAC frames can be larger than that. Gecko reads up to 8096 bytes for ADTS ([bug 1787159](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1787159), [`nsMediaSniffer.cpp`](https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/cac25a6fa321b0051932359b84c4e2fe3caabdc5/toolkit/components/mediasniffer/nsMediaSniffer.cpp#36-38)).\n\nORB (whatwg/fetch#1755) runs the audio or video type pattern matching algorithm on the first 1024 bytes, so it's affected too.\n\nMaybe the audio or video type pattern matching algorithm could read up to 8096 bytes for ADTS, as Gecko does?",
